@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Validated account backup restore with a safety copy
hide footbox
autonumber
actor User
participant "WorkspaceSettings\n<<React function>>" as Web
participant "workspace_backups.py\n<<routes / functions>>" as Backup
participant "workspace : WorkspaceStore" as Store
participant "Private filesystem" as Files

activate User
User -> Web : select ZIP and request preview
activate Web
Web -> Backup : POST /backups/preview\ncookie + Origin + CSRF
activate Backup
note over Backup : Authenticated account context precedes this domain interaction.
Backup -> Backup : validate size/paths/hashes/media;\nnormalize workspace format 1 or validate format 2
activate Backup
Backup --> Backup : validated document or rejection
deactivate Backup
opt valid archive
  Backup -> Files : publish bounded preview ZIP atomically
  activate Files
  Files --> Backup : staged or explicit I/O error
  deactivate Files
  opt archive staged
    Backup -> Store : read version and record expiring owner-scoped preview
    activate Store
    Store --> Backup : version / preview metadata
    deactivate Store
  end
end
Backup --> Web : counts, warnings, token and version, or error
deactivate Backup
Web --> User : inspect replacement scope
deactivate Web

User -> Web : type REPLACE and confirm
activate Web
Web -> Backup : POST /backups/restore\n{token, expected_version, confirmation}
activate Backup
Backup -> Store : acquire account lock; verify token and version
activate Store
Store --> Backup : current snapshot or conflict
deactivate Store
alt preview valid and workspace unchanged
  Backup -> Files : reread and validate staged archive
  activate Files
  Files --> Backup : valid archive or rejection
  deactivate Files
  Backup -> Backup : snapshot current workspace as pre-restore backup
  activate Backup
  Backup --> Backup : verified safety backup ID or failure
  deactivate Backup
  opt safety snapshot and archive validation succeeded
    Backup -> Files : stage immutable audio; remap conflicting names
    activate Files
    Files --> Backup : staged files or error
    deactivate Files
    alt audio staged
    Backup -> Store : import_document(document, expected_version)\nprojects/entries/revisions/history/coursework/screenshots
    activate Store
    Store --> Backup : committed new version or rolled-back SQL transaction
    deactivate Store
    alt logical data committed
      Backup -> Store : invalidate preview token
      activate Store
      Store --> Backup : token removed
      deactivate Store
      Backup -> Files : remove used preview
      activate Files
      Files --> Backup : cleaned up or explicit error
      deactivate Files
    else logical commit failed
      Backup -> Files : remove only newly staged audio
      activate Files
      Files --> Backup : original committed media retained
      deactivate Files
    end
    else audio staging failed
      Backup -> Files : remove only newly staged audio
      activate Files
      Files --> Backup : original committed media retained
      deactivate Files
    end
  end
else expired preview or changed workspace
  note over Backup : Reject without logical replacement; user must preview again.
end
note over Backup, Store : Release account lock on exit.\nNever report a failed/uncertain commit as success.
Backup --> Web : restored counts + safety ID, or explicit error
deactivate Backup
Web --> User : reopen General and review restored content,\nor preserve error/recovery guidance
deactivate Web
deactivate User
legend bottom
  Backups replace logical workspace data, not account credentials or server settings.
  Workspace document format 2 includes profile JSON and screenshot base64; outer manifest stays format 1.
  Older format-1 documents normalize to empty coursework/screenshots before replacement.
  Profile/screenshot mutations invalidate a previously captured expected_version.
  Late client cancellation does not promise server rollback.
  Existing committed media remains available for recovery; this is not a cross-file ACID transaction.
endlegend
@enduml
